# A journey is a passage of the journal: setting out, the meeting on the road, the fight, the arrival.
#
# Travel and a roadside fight have no narration, so before this the journal kept only the fight's
# milestone, in a group with nothing the chronicler could write from. The game now writes events of
# its own (JournalRecorder.Event): where the party set out from and for, who barred the way, and on
# arrival the lands crossed and how long it took — and the journey's group closes there, before the
# visit opens, so it is written up as its own passage "on the road".
#
# --encounter-on-arrival puts the wolf on the last step; fight-end settles the fight without blows
# (journal_fight_blows.cli covers those).
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --encounter-on-arrival wolf --no-chronicler

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60

travel neighbour
travel-go

wait mode EncounterPrompt 90
inspect journal
expect-state journal set out from the
expect-state journal barred the way

click engage
wait mode Fighting 90
fight-end victory
wait mode LocationInteraction 90

inspect journal
expect-state journal kind=Event state=Pending
expect-state journal Won a fight against
expect-state journal reached the
expect-state journal pending-groups=1
save roundtrip

quit
